{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>from the impurity of the children of Israel.</b> For those who entered the Sanctuary in impurity and it was not known to them in the end, as it says <b>for all their sins</b> — and a sin is unintentional." "<b>and their transgressions.</b> Also those who enter intentionally in impurity (ibid. 7)." "<b>And so he shall do for the Tent of Meeting.</b> Just as he sprinkled from both of them inside — once above and seven below, so he sprinkles upon the curtain from outside from both of them — once above and seven below (Sifra; Yoma 56)." "<b>who dwells among them in the midst of their impurity.</b> Even though they are impure — the Shechinah is among them (ibid.)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:46.938457325Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}